    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/2002.01968v2</id>
    <title>Avoidance of split overlaps</title>
    <updated>2020-02-25T22:17:31Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2002.01968v2" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2002.01968v2" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>We generalize Axel Thue's familiar definition of overlaps in words, and show that there are no infinite words containing split occurrences of these generalized overlaps. Along the way we prove a useful theorem about repeated disjoint occurrences in words -- an interesting natural variation on the classical de Bruijn sequences.</summary>
